    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 **58 run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `Cp46Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI converted owner deletion to a soft-delete across the stack:\n\n**Domain / persistence**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added a `deleted` field (`Boolean`, default `false`) with `@Column(name = \"deleted\")` and getter/setter, so a newly instantiated/created owner is `deleted = false`.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql` \u2014 added a `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` column to the `owners` table (hsqldb is what the tests run against; the others updated for parity). Seed inserts use explicit column lists, so they default to `false`.\n\n**API contract**\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema (and to its `required` list), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the flag and MapStruct maps `Owner.deleted \u2192 OwnerDto.deleted` automatically. It appears in GET/create responses.\n\n**Controller behavior** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`)\n- `deleteOwner` now sets `deleted = true` and persists via `saveOwner` instead of removing the row \u2014 still returns `204` (2xx). `GET /api/owners/{id}` continues to find the retained record and now reports `deleted: true`.\n- The create endpoint's duplicate/identity checks \u2014 `rejectDuplicateIdentity`, `rejectHouseholdDuplicate`, and `assignPossibleDuplicate` \u2014 now filter out soft-deleted owners (`!isDeleted(existing)`), so a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only matching owner has been deleted. Added a small `isDeleted` helper.\n\nThe two new acceptance tests (soft-delete flags-and-retains, and deleted-owner-ignored-by-duplicate-check) pass, and all 56 pre-existing tests remain green.",
